      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Absolutely unacceptable. I'm having this issue and to learn that it's been a thing for a few months to a year now with no fix in sight? That's not cool at all. Everything on my computer for Windows 10 is updated as far as I trust it to be and as far as compatible with my hardware build. It's the time out for launching EAC and VRChat that's the problem. It's very problematic and I shouldn't be dealing with a roll of the dice every time I try to launch VRChat. When it doesn't run into this issue it's fine but when it does, the whole computer has a bsod with a security kernel issue. Maybe the team for VRChat should have thought this through first and found the more secure method to combat avatar ripping, etc.\n\nAnd like I would like to tack on, as another user had said here, this is clearly an issue with the EOS version of EAC because I don't even have this BSOD issue with Fortnite nor Halo MCC. If you want to still use EAC, try using not the EOS but the basic EAC version.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
